# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.venv/

# storyboard.py / storyline.py generated output — regenerable, and some
# embed base64 video/image data that shouldn't sit in version control.
# Anchored to the repo root so it doesn't also catch hand-authored
# index.html files elsewhere (e.g. catalog/index.html).
/storyboard.html
/storyboard_*.html
/storyline_*.html
/index.html
*.notes.json
*.feedback.json

# HyperFrames per-project local state/caches (regenerable; absent from every
# video/*/ project committed so far — preview server state, media-resolution
# ledger, thumbnail cache, waveform cache, transcode cache).
.hyperframes/
.media/
.thumbnails/
.waveform-cache/
.transcode-cache/

# npm dependencies inside each video/*/ project — never committed so far,
# reinstalled from package.json/package-lock.json instead.
node_modules/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# HyperFrames render scratch. `hyperframes render` writes per-worker capture
# frames into renders/work-<uuid>/ for the whole duration of a render, so a
# 6-minute 1080p render is a ~15-minute window in which any broad `git add` in
# a project directory sweeps them into the commit. That is a property of the
# tool, not of any one video, which is why these live at the repo root.
#
# Cost of not having this: one session committed 6,844 capture frames, 556 MB,
# via `git add -A` while a render was in flight. Caught only because the branch
# happened to be under review before pushing; on origin it would have needed a
# history rewrite to remove.
videos/*/renders/work-*/
videos/*/renders/.*hf-transaction*

# scripts/gen_vo.py --from-takes staging cache (concatenated source takes +
# their raw ASR transcripts, keyed by scene id) -- regenerable from the
# committed per-scene takes, not canonical project output.
videos/*/assets/voice/acts/_takes/

# Retention-master plate sources (raw generator downloads, 9MB PNGs / 2.5K MP4s);
# the prepared 1080p plates next to them are what the composition references.
videos/*/assets/plates/raw/
.ci-local/
